WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.330
50,000 "Witcher" fans can't be wrong.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.710
Or can they?

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:10.854
Here's how some of the show's most loyal watchers
are trying to keep the dream of a Henry Cavill-led "Witcher" alive.

00:00:10.854 --> 00:00:15.350
Fans of Netflix's "The Witcher" are still
reeling from the recent news that Cavill will

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:19.000
no longer be donning his iconic white wig
after Season 3.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.449
"Enjoy your last walk across the meadow, and
through the mist."

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:28.170
Cavill has officially laid down his swords
as Geralt of Rivia and will instead be picking

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.859
up that iconic red cape once again.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:34.590
Some have speculated that the actor's departure
from the Netflix series was due to incompatible

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.560
work schedules.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.350
Without a doubt, fighting crime and the forces
of evil as Superman is an intensive and time-consuming

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.430
position to be in.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.710
Not to mention that, in all likelihood, being
part of the DC Universe pays better than acting

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:46.472
on "The Witcher."

00:00:46.472 --> 00:00:50.640
However, many fans aren't too happy that Cavill
won't be returning to the role, and will be

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.559
replaced by Australian actor (and brother
to Thor) Liam Hemsworth.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:59.519
Out of all this discontentment, a Change.org
petition emerged, similar to what happened

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:01.760
after "Game of Thrones" Season 8 aired.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.340
The petition titled "NETFLIX: You MUST keep
Henry Cavill as The Witcher and replace the

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:12.030
writers instead" has blown up, and, as of
the making of this video, it has nearly reached

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.900
its goal of 50,000 signatures.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.390
Stef Ma, the creator of the petition, wrote,
in part,

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:21.210
"Let us show them in pure numbers [...] that
none of us Witcher fans will stand with them

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:26.090
and will abandon the show (and potentially
our subscriptions) after The Witcher season

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:27.270
3 is concluded."

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.439
Unfortunately, this puts Liam Hemsworth, who
can’t be blamed for the recasting, in an

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:32.930
unfavorable position.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.869
On an Instagram post, the Australian actor
acknowledged that Cavill handed him the reins

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:41.470
of the series' beloved protagonist, and while
some commenters showed their support, many

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.649
others expressed their displeasure.

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:48.090
One of the top comments with over 5,000 likes
reads, "no. stop.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.320
you can't replace henry"

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.020
"Witcher" fans have been quite vocal about
their opposition to the major change all over

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.020
the internet.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.880
On Reddit, there are multiple threads about
the recasting.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:58.880
One user wrote,

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.170
"Well, there goes the single redeeming factor
of the show."

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.930
This got several replies, including,

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:08.860
"I actually really like Joey Batey [...] The
bard song is cool, and his character is slowly

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.170
developing rather nicely.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.841
But yeah, other than that, you're totally
right."

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:14.141
"I'm going to drink.

00:02:14.141 --> 00:02:17.203
I am not having this conversation unless I'm
drinking."

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:21.489
Indeed, one should not discredit the other
actors who have also fully dedicated themselves

00:02:21.489 --> 00:02:25.170
to the series like Batey, Anya Chalotra, and
Freya Allan.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.870
However, together they don’t seem to be
enough to relieve fans' doubts regarding the

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.280
future of the series.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:35.269
During his three seasons on "The Witcher,"
Henry Cavill seemed born to play Geralt of Rivia.

00:02:35.269 --> 00:02:40.650
This was, in great part, thanks to the incredible
passion Cavill nurtured for the fantasy franchise,

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:45.330
first as a fan of the video games and later
as a fan of Andrzej Sapkowski's novels.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.290
In an interview with Graham Norton, Cavill
was asked whether he knew more than anyone

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.290
else on set.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:55.149
Ever humble, Cavill denied knowing more than
anyone else and just called himself a "big fan."

00:02:55.149 --> 00:02:59.478
Norton then asked whether he corrected others
on set, to which Cavill replied that he doesn't,

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:00.103
adding,

00:03:00.103 --> 00:03:07.385
"I am effusive about getting, about being
loyal to the source material, let's put it that way."

00:03:07.385 --> 00:03:11.440
Those are the operative words: "loyal to the
source material."

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.379
It has somewhat become common knowledge even
among those who haven't read the books that

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:20.098
the Netflix show, especially after the first
season, strayed from Sapkowski's original story.

00:03:20.098 --> 00:03:24.790
Although Cavill has never outright said it,
his comments to Norton suggest that he might

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:28.819
not have been content with the direction the
series had taken, ultimately leading to him

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:30.659
stepping down as the monster hunter.

